Workshop focus: 
===============
Client/Server applications are of increasing interest in industry; they are 
an important first step towards a global distributed processing model. 
A very current response to this trend is the Distributed Computing 
Environment (DCE) of the Open Software Foundation (OSF) as an emerging 
industry standard for distributed processing.

This workshop will discuss the client/server approach based on DCE, 
illustrating and analyzing the functionality of important DCE components 
and applications.

Moreover, the workshop will focus on new models beyond traditional 
client/server processing and beyond DCE. As typical examples, distributed 
object-oriented approaches, the Object Request Broker (ORB) of the Object 
Management Group (OMG), as well as dedicated extensions of RPC functionality 
will be important topics.

The workshop will bring together practicitioners and researchers in the area 
of distributed systems. The international program covers a representative set 
of fields related to DCE technology and distributed processing models. 
Furthermore, an exhibition provides practical information on DCE and its 
technology.

