In <1993Jun2.142657.5218@muug.mb.ca> rbuskens@muug.mb.ca (Rob Buskens) writes:
>If DCE replaces NIS for network login verification then does it also
>replace the rest of the facilities that NIS provides?

DCE source from OSF includes a login program that speaks to the DCE
security server(s).  We want vendors to take that program, add to it
as needed, and have a unified login.  The security server also includes
the traditional /etc/passwd information.  There are tools to import
and export passwd files, and to have a local /etc/passwd with bits and
pieces that override the security server's cell-wide data (e.g., to have
per-machine root passwords).

The rest of NIS is either unchanged (mail aliases), not recommended (use
DNS instead of host maps and NIS domains) or will eventually become
obsolete (:-).
