>(BTW, I'd be really grateful if someone could explain the rationale for having to
>associate Type UUIDs with Object UUIDs when you wish to select from multiple
>services within a single server.  There seems to be a an unnecessary level of
>indirection, or am I missing something?)

I'm not sure what you mean by this.  You only need a Type UUID if you have
multiple instances of the same interface.  Suppose we have a printer
interface that provides a "print_text" operation.  For a PostScript
printer we have to translate the text, while for a daisy wheel we just
send it out.  This means we have two different implementations of the same
operation.  If a server manages several printers, they will group each
printer into the appropriate type.  When a print_text operation is
received, the RPC runtime will automatically invoke the PostScript or the
Daisy version.  If, later on, you upgrade your printer, then the server
just has to change the type for the new printer, and existing clients
will now get nice Daisy :-) output without any changes at all.

Make sense?
	/r$


