In <1993Jun7.151247.2332@walter.bellcore.com> grd@scherzo.bellcore.com (Glen Diener) writes:
>X cannot, for example, link both the client stub,
>the server stub, and a method definition for ping()...the method
>definition will end up clashing with a definition for ping in
>the  client stub, and produce a multiply-defined symbol at link time.

You should be able to do this by doing the following:
    -	Write your "ping" operation implementation, but call it
	something like my_ping_op or some such.
    -	Take a look at the generated server_stub file and pull out
	the manager_epv part -- it will be a custom structure that
	has one function pointer for each operation.
    -	Copy the variable (separating the variable from its typedef
	may be tricky :-) into one of your server source files and replace
	"ping" with my_ping_op.
    -	Run IDL with the -no_mepv flag.
Compile and link as normal.


