In <1v29gu$efa@rag.austin.nam.slb.com> khan@asc.slb.com (Naved Khan) writes:
>        Does anyone know if DCE RPC allows the remote procedures to
>have variable number of arguments?

If you mean something like stdargs or varargs, then the answer is that
it cannot be done.  If you think about it, you can see that it would
require the IDL stub routine to do the same analysis that the operation
routine would have to do in order to determine the number and type of
arguments.  Even then, you could make mistakes:
	char *p = "my text";
	printf("%s is at %x", p, p);
How would you know that P should be sent over once as a string, and the
second time as a pointer?  (Yes, this code isn't 100% portable but you
get the idea.)
	/r$


